# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
#
# luofu-shrink.fragment - the kernelb size budget for the own-kernel image.
#
# The un-shrunk image (multi_v7_defconfig + luofu.fragment) is a 10,142,208 B
# zImage / 10,142,272 B uImage + a 10,807 B DTB = 10,153,079 B slice, i.e.
# 1,502,327 B MORE than the 8,650,752-byte kernelb partition (mtd12) - the
# abort recorded in build/tmp/inta-spec/firstkboot.md. The vendor's own slice
# uses only 4,334,892 B of that same partition, so the overflow is the fat
# multi-platform base (30+ mach-* directories, 110 platform symbols), not the
# partition.
#
# This fragment is the shrink. It is applied ON TOP of the same base and
# luofu.fragment, so it can only switch OFF what is listed here - nothing else
# moves, and anything a kept symbol still selects comes back on its own
# (`make olddefconfig` decides). Apply (host-side only, like luofu.fragment):
#   make ARCH=arm multi_v7_defconfig
#   scripts/kconfig/merge_config.sh -m .config lab/luofu-kernel/luofu.fragment \
#       lab/luofu-kernel/luofu-shrink.fragment
#   make ARCH=arm olddefconfig
#
# What stays: what the boot actually needs. The machine (ARCH_HISI + ARCH_LUOFU
# + the luofu DTB), the ARM core (GIC, architected timer, L2X0 + its errata,
# MULTIPLATFORM/OF/SPARSE_IRQ/IRQ_DOMAIN), the console (SERIAL_8250_DW +
# SERIAL_8250_CONSOLE -> SERIAL_EARLYCON; no VT, the boot console is ttyS0),
# the storage and mount path (MTD + MTD_SPI_NAND + MTD_UBI[_BLOCK] + SQUASHFS +
# UBIFS_FS + EXT4), the pstore pair (PSTORE/PSTORE_CONSOLE/PSTORE_RAM), PCI +
# PCIEPORTBUS (the two DWC root complexes), CFG80211/MAC80211 (the wifi work),
# plain userspace (DEVTMPFS/PROC_FS/SYSFS/TMPFS/BINFMT_ELF/UNIX98_PTYS) and the
# TTY/printk/KALLSYMS/STACKTRACE machinery that makes a panic readable.
# The lane .github/workflows/luofu-kernel-config.yml asserts that list and
# fails the build on an over-budget uImage, so this file cannot silently rot.
#
# What goes: every other SoC's mach/plat code, the whole non-luofu driver
# surface (USB/MMC/DRM/FB/audio/media/input/hwmon/BT/SCSI/ATA/sensors), every
# filesystem we do not mount, netfilter/traffic-control/bridging, the other
# MAC/PHY/WLAN drivers, the on-chip peripheral drivers whose bindings this DT
# does not use, and the optional debug/perf/ftrace/EFI/keys machinery. Symbols
# the base carries as =m (modules) are left alone: `zImage dtbs` builds no
# modules, so they cost the image nothing.
#
# Size-oriented: CC_OPTIMIZE_FOR_SIZE (+ FOR_PERFORMANCE off) and no initramfs
# (BLK_DEV_INITRD=n - the RD_* unpackers fall away with it).
#
# Rule followed throughout (same as luofu.fragment): no trailing comments on a
# CONFIG_ line - merge_config.sh compares whole lines.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# kept explicitly: symbols the base config only had because OTHER platforms or
# drivers selected them. With 30+ platforms gone these would silently fall off
# (`make olddefconfig` cannot re-derive them), and each one is load-bearing
# here: HAVE_ARM_ARCH_TIMER is the ARM architected timer (the only clocksource
# this board has), VFP/NEON are userspace floating point and the NEON unit,
# I2C/TMPFS/STACKTRACE/PM/HIGHMEM/THERMAL_OF are framework bits the fragment
# and the console rely on, and the ARM_ERRATA_* / PL310_ERRATA_* are the
# Cortex-A9 + PL310 workarounds that other boards' Kconfig entries used to
# select for us. All 23 are prompted symbols (a fragment can only set prompted
# ones - the removed multi_v7 platforms had selected the rest).
CONFIG_HAVE_ARM_ARCH_TIMER=y
CONFIG_VFP=y
CONFIG_NEON=y
CONFIG_HIGHMEM=y
CONFIG_PM=y
CONFIG_VDSO=y
CONFIG_I2C=y
CONFIG_STACKTRACE=y
CONFIG_TMPFS=y
CONFIG_THERMAL_OF=y
CONFIG_ARM_ERRATA_430973=y
CONFIG_ARM_ERRATA_643719=y
CONFIG_ARM_ERRATA_720789=y
CONFIG_ARM_ERRATA_754322=y
CONFIG_ARM_ERRATA_754327=y
CONFIG_ARM_ERRATA_764369=y
CONFIG_ARM_ERRATA_775420=y
CONFIG_ARM_ERRATA_798181=y
CONFIG_ARM_ERRATA_814220=y
CONFIG_PL310_ERRATA_588369=y
CONFIG_PL310_ERRATA_727915=y
CONFIG_PL310_ERRATA_753970=y
CONFIG_PL310_ERRATA_769419=y


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# size-oriented build options
# The slice's kernel half is a zImage (self-decompressing) inside a comp=none
# uImage, so kernel compression (-Os + gzip) is the cheapest lever there is;
# and the kernelb slice carries no initramfs, so the unpackers are dead weight.
CONFIG_CC_OPTIMIZE_FOR_SIZE=y
# CONFIG_CC_OPTIMIZE_FOR_PERFORMANCE is not set
# CONFIG_BLK_DEV_INITRD is not set

